            <td height="39"> 
              <div align="center"> 
                <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="5" align="center"><b> 
                  Dick Armey's call for war crimes should not go unreported and 
                  unanswered </b></font></p>
              </div>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr align="left" valign="top"> 
            <td height="2"> 
              <hr height="1">
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr align="left" valign="top"> 
            <td height="1603"> 
              <p> 
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> <b>PMWATCH 
                - May 6, 2002</b> --<font size="3"> On May 1, 2002, as a guest 
                of MSNBC's Hardball with Chris Matthews (<a href="#TRANSCRIPT">see 
                transcript below</a>), House Republican Majority Leader Dick Armey 
                (R-TX) spoke on the record for the transfer of Palestinian populations 
                from the West Bank and Gaza to other Arab countries and the permanent 
                annexation of those lands by Israel. (See action calls from <a href="http://www.cair-net.org" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">CAIR</a>, 
                <a href="http://www.adc.org" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">ADC</a>, along with an article from 
                Ahmed Amr of <a href="http://www.nilemedia.com" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">NileMedia.com</a>)</font></font></p>
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> It has now 
                been five days since Dick Armey (Rep. Texas) said on the record: 
                "I'm content to have Israel grab the entire West Bank" and "There 
                are many Arab nations that have many hundreds of thousands of 
                acres of land". </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> Since then, 
                nothing by way of a reaction has been forthcoming from the otherwise 
                moralizing media. The Majority Leader calls for ethnic cleansing 
                -- technically an act of Genocide (see below) -- and it simply 
                does not make the news, let alone elicit editorials of outrage. 
                </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> Exhibit A 
                -- the full transcript of Dick Armey's remarks is at: <a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/pmw/cast/armey.asp#TRANSCRIPT">http://www.pmwatch.org/pmw/cast/armey.asp#TRANSCRIPT</a> 
                </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> You can cite 
                the Geneva Conventions at: <a href="http://www.hrweb.org/legal/undocs.html" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">http://www.hrweb.org/legal/undocs.html</a> 
                </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> Specifically, 
                Article 12 says: </font>
              </p><p> 
              </p><pre><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">1. Everyone lawfully within the territory of a 
   State shall, within that territory, have the 
   right to liberty of movement and freedom to 
   choose his residence. 

2. Everyone shall be free to leave any country, 
   including his own. 

3. The above-mentioned rights shall not be subject 
   to any restrictions except those which are provided 
   by law, are necessary to protect national 
   security, public order (ordre public), public 
   health or morals or the rights and freedoms of 
   others, and are consistent with the other rights 
   recognized in the present Covenant. 

4. No one shall be arbitrarily deprived of the right 
   to enter his own country. 
</font></pre>
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> Dick Armey's 
                call DIRECTLY violates at least (1) and (4) </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> You can also 
                cite: "Convention on the Prevention and Punishment of the Crime 
                of Genocide" -- <a href="http://www.hrweb.org/legal/genocide.html#Article%202" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">http://www.hrweb.org/legal/genocide.html#Article%202</a> 
                </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> Article 2 
                says: "In the present Convention, genocide means any of the following 
                acts committed with intent to destroy, in whole or in part, a 
                national, ethnical, racial or religious group, as such: </font>
              </p><p> 
              </p><pre><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">
	(a) Killing members of the group; 
	(b) Causing serious bodily or mental harm to
            members of the group; 
	(c) Deliberately inflicting on the group 
            conditions of life calculated to 
	    bring about its physical destruction in 
            whole or in part; 
	(d) Imposing measures intended to prevent 
            births within the group; 
	(e) Forcibly transferring children of the 
            group to another group." 
</font></pre>
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> Dick Armey 
                is OPENLY promoting at least (e). </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> Article 3 
                says: </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> The following 
                acts shall be punishable: </font>
              </p><p> 
              </p><pre><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">
	(a) Genocide; 
	(b) Conspiracy to commit genocide; 
	(c) Direct and public incitement to commit 
            genocide; 
	(d) Attempt to commit genocide; 
	(e) Complicity in genocide. 
</font></pre>
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> Dick Armey 
                is CLEARLY guilty of at least (c). </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> The Convention 
                further states: "People suspected of acts of genocide may be tried 
                by a national tribunal in the territory where the acts were committed 
                or by a properly constituted international tribunal whose jurisdiction 
                is recognized by the state or states involved. For purposes of 
                extradition, an allegation of genocide is not to be considered 
                a political crime, and states are bound to extradite suspects 
                in accordance with national laws and treaties. Any state party 
                to the Convention may also call upon the United Nations to act 
                to prevent or punish acts of genocide." </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> Specifically, 
                Article 6 says: "Persons charged with genocide or any of the other 
                acts enumerated in Article 3 shall be tried by a competent tribunal 
                of the State in the territory of which the act was committed, 
                or by such international penal tribunal as may have jurisdiction 
                with respect to those Contracting Parties which shall have accepted 
                its jurisdiction." </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> In other 
                words, in addition to the clear moral breach by Mr. Armey, there 
                are also CLEAR grounds for bringing Dick Armey to court for incitement 
                of Genocide. </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> Press contact 
                info is at: <a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/pmw/volunteer/calling.html">http://www.pmwatch.org/pmw/volunteer/calling.html</a> 
                </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> Thanks and 
                let's keep pushing. I am going to see if any group is interested 
                in filing a legal complaint against Armey and start something 
                that hopefully will wildly go out of control just on the technicalities 
                of it (just as Pinochet got the scare and the humiliation of his 
                life because of judges in Portugal and the UK had to follow rules 
                and regulations and procedures...) </font> 
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> </font><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">Your 
                letter will be sent to:</font> 
              </p><pre><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">
